# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: 'Registrar: add lock and unlock'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      `pallet-registrar-para::add_lock` shuts the manager out of a registered para; `remove_lock`
      lifts it, for root or the para itself only. Both emit an event, where the relay chain's lock
      was silent. `ParaInfo` grows a `locked` flag, and a new `ParachainOrigin` config type lets a
      para act as itself.

      `pallet-registrar-relay::authorize_code` and `cancel_authorization` are merged into a single
      `receive` at call index 0, the way the parachain side already takes every report through one
      call. The message enum decides what happens, so the transport no longer has to pick a call
      index per variant, and the `UnexpectedMessage` error is gone. Weights split per variant:
      `receive_register` and `receive_cancel_registration`.

crates:
  - name: pallet-registrar-para
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-relay
    bump: major
